            <ArticleTitle>Leadership for Addressing Aging in America: The Health and Aging Policy Fellowship.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>819-825</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1525-8610(17)30379-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jamda.2017.07.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Health and Aging Policy Fellows Program funded by The John A. Hartford Foundation and Atlantic Philanthropies trains future leaders to influence healthcare policy, systems, and program development in aging. Following a rigorous residential training in Washington, DC, Fellows establish placements of up to 1 year in the executive, legislative, or judicial branch of government, at a federal agency, state or community agency or committee, or with a nongovernmental organization. The 2016-2017 Fellows' activities represent a broad scope of work, including contributions to national and local policy priorities expected to build over time far beyond the core fellowship year.</AbstractText>
